<Layout title="Documentation" active="docs"><section class="wrap section prose"><div class="eyebrow">Getting started</div><h1>Run RackChief locally.</h1><p class="muted">The authenticated application runs with Docker Compose and a hosted Supabase project.</p><h2>Prerequisites</h2><p>Install Git, Docker Compose, and access to the configured Supabase development project.</p><h2>Clone and configure</h2><div class="code">git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/RackChief/RackChief.git · cd RackChief · cp .env.example .env</div><p>Fill in <code>DATABASE_URL</code>, <code>SUPABASE_URL</code>, <code>SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY</code>, and <code>SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY</code>.</p><h2>Start the application</h2><div class="code">docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up --build</div><p>Open <code>http://localhost:5173</code>. The REST API is under <code>/api/v1</code>, OpenAPI is at <code>/openapi.json</code>, and MCP is at <code>/mcp</code>.</p></section></Layout>
